Nobody tells the policy to think longer; it learns to because longer answers are the ones that earn reward, and only where they do (@fig-grpo). Easy problems stay short (2\.6 steps on average at the end), medium ones settle at 4\.1 and hard ones at 7\.9, while every accuracy ends above 0\.88. Hard problems start late: the policy first has to stumble on a long enough answer inside a group.

